silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#mittensdiagramimage a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.06_topology_jepa.chapters.flat.sections.01_thesis.concrete_anchor#mittensdiagramimage" .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#mittensdiagramimage silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensDiagramImage is the rendered image of the Mittens olog diagram (head, torso, paws, tail, body-mass 4.2 kg tag, vet-record stamp, Cat-classification arrow) input to the topology-JEPA pipeline. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'I_Mittens', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#headpatch a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.06_topology_jepa.chapters.flat.sections.01_thesis.concrete_anchor#headpatch" .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#headpatch silm:hasLongDescription "The HeadPatch is the rectangular pixel window covering the head region of Mittens-the-cat in the diagram, including the cat-classification node and its outgoing Cat arrow. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'U_head', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#bodypatch a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.06_topology_jepa.chapters.flat.sections.01_thesis.concrete_anchor#bodypatch" .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#bodypatch silm:hasLongDescription "The BodyPatch is the rectangular pixel window covering the torso of Mittens including the BodyMass 4.2 kg quality node and its measurement arrow. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'U_body', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#tailpatch a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.06_topology_jepa.chapters.flat.sections.01_thesis.concrete_anchor#tailpatch" .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#tailpatch silm:hasLongDescription "The TailPatch is the rectangular pixel window covering the tail of Mittens including the 28cm length tag and the white-tuft marking. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'U_tail', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#overlapzone a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.06_topology_jepa.chapters.flat.sections.01_thesis.concrete_anchor#overlapzone" .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#overlapzone silm:hasLongDescription "The OverlapZone is the shared pixel region where the head patch and body patch both cover the neck-joint region of Mittens, requiring agreement on the apex glyph. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'U_overlap', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#headlocalhypothesis a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.06_topology_jepa.chapters.flat.sections.01_thesis.concrete_anchor#headlocalhypothesis" .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#headlocalhypothesis silm:hasLongDescription "The HeadLocalHypothesis is the local olog hypothesis for the head patch: cat-classification node plus outgoing Cat morphism, signed by Dr. Osei in the May 2026 Tartu Animal Clinic record. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'D_head', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#bodylocalhypothesis a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.06_topology_jepa.chapters.flat.sections.01_thesis.concrete_anchor#bodylocalhypothesis" .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#bodylocalhypothesis silm:hasLongDescription "The BodyLocalHypothesis is the local olog hypothesis for the body patch: BodyMass:4.2kg quality node plus the typed measurement arrow from scale-witness WeightMeas to Mittens. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'D_body', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#assembledmittensgraph a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.06_topology_jepa.chapters.flat.sections.01_thesis.concrete_anchor#assembledmittensgraph" .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#assembledmittensgraph silm:hasLongDescription "The AssembledMittensGraph is the assembled global typed graph for Mittens-the-cat, the colimit apex receiving all typed-leg cocone legs from local patch hypotheses. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'G_Mittens', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#vetcareplanrecord a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.06_topology_jepa.chapters.flat.sections.01_thesis.concrete_anchor#vetcareplanrecord" .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#vetcareplanrecord silm:hasLongDescription "The VetCarePlanRecord is the clinical care plan record 77 generated for Mittens at the May 2026 vet visit, a competing cocone target also receiving the typed legs. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'VetCarePlan_77', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#encoderfunctor a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.06_topology_jepa.chapters.flat.sections.01_thesis.concrete_anchor#encoderfunctor" .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#encoderfunctor silm:hasLongDescription "The EncoderFunctor is the JEPA context encoder realized as a structure-preserving functor from the image-patch category to the latent hypothesis category. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'E_encoder', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#predictortransformation a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.06_topology_jepa.chapters.flat.sections.01_thesis.concrete_anchor#predictortransformation" .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#predictortransformation silm:hasLongDescription "The PredictorTransformation is the JEPA predictor realized as a natural transformation between two encoder functor profiles, predicting target-patch latents from context. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'P_predictor', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#tracewitness a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.06_topology_jepa.chapters.flat.sections.01_thesis.concrete_anchor#tracewitness" .
silm:instances_papers_06_topology_jepa_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#tracewitness silm:hasLongDescription "The TraceWitness is the outgoing Yoneda profile trace from G_Mittens, the SHACL-conformant GraphJSON serialization with vet-record provenance line included. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'T_trace', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
